hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22872","Abdur-Rahman narrated to us: Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn al-Harith, from Haram ibn Muawiyah, from his uncle Abdullah ibn Sad, who said: I asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about eating with a menstruating woman, so he said: Eat with her."
"22873","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, who said: I heard Abu al-Bakhtari at-Tai, who said: One who heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, informed me, saying: People will not perish until they excuse themselves from themselves."
"22874","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Ibn al-Mubarak informed us: Abdur-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir narrated to us, who said: Said ibn Abi Said narrated to me, from one who heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Lo, indeed a borrowed item is to be returned, and a granted milch animal is to be given back, and a debt is to be settled, and the guarantor is liable."
